/-
# L5Reg.Reg1323 : the lines clause for every class of the local table of rep #1323 (generated by l5reg)

Every local class `i < nT` of rep #1323 (133 classes) is matched to the lines record `(chunk, index)` of `adv` with a 3x3 integer matrix `M` (UNTRUSTED advice): the kernel checks
`G l'_i = sum_k M_ik l_k` (G from digits 1..10 of the record), the signed-permutation property of G, and that every local range lies in a record range (`L5Reg.Equiv.eqChk`).
The theorem takes, for each chunk used, the lines clause of the chunk's records (from `Lin.lines_clause_tab` via `L5Reg.Mem`).
No `sorry`, no `native_decide`, no new axiom.  Not registered in any aggregator.
-/
